{
  "description": "Cross-SDK vectors for AI agents. thumbprints: RFC 7638 JWK thumbprints (the default kid; RFC 9449 §6 and RFC 8037 A.3 examples). ath: base64url SHA-256 of an access token, as a DPoP proof carries it (RFC 9449 §7.1 example). calls: what each management call sends; \"{id}\" is the agent created by the first call, \"{kid}\" the kid of its second key. approvalToken: an approval token signed by the jwks key (verify at now = verifyAt), with a tampered copy and one of the wrong type. matching: which `expect` values match a token's authorization_details (amounts compare as decimals, IBANs without spaces and case-insensitively, currencies case-insensitively; every expected field must be equal, extra fields are ignored; an array matches entry by entry).",
